Blocks the handlePayflowProResponse GraphQL mutation while Payflow Pro is disabled.

Root cause: Magento\PaypalGraphQl\Model\Resolver\PayflowProResponse is the GraphQL twin of
Magento\Paypal\Controller\Transparent\Response, and it carries the same omission - it never checks
whether Payflow Pro is actually active before running ResponseValidator::validate(). The validator's
default branch throws "Transaction has been declined" for any payload that is not a valid Payflow
response, and the resolver passes that straight to PaymentFailuresInterface::handle(), which emails
the admin a "Payment Failed" notification rendered from the attacker-controlled quote billing address.

The mutation accepts a guest masked cart id, so it is reachable unauthenticated over POST /graphql
with no form key and no CSRF token. Patching only the frontend controller therefore leaves an
equivalent, equally unauthenticated path open, and /graphql cannot be blocked at the web server
because the storefront and integrations depend on it.

Fix: apply the same guard used by Magento\Paypal\Controller\Transparent\RequestSecureToken, rejecting
the mutation with a GraphQlInputException before the cart is loaded and before any payment failure
notification can be triggered. Shops that genuinely run Payflow Pro are unaffected. No new constructor
dependency and no new import are required - the Transparent model is already injected and
GraphQlInputException is already imported.

diff --git a/Model/Resolver/PayflowProResponse.php b/Model/Resolver/PayflowProResponse.php
index 29a0a31..a6b18bf 100644
--- a/Model/Resolver/PayflowProResponse.php
+++ b/Model/Resolver/PayflowProResponse.php
@@ -118,6 +118,13 @@ class PayflowProResponse implements ResolverInterface
 
         $maskedCartId = $args['input']['cart_id'];
         $storeId = (int)$context->getExtensionAttributes()->getStore()->getId();
+
+        // BEGIN PATCH
+        if (!$this->transparent->isActive($storeId)) {
+            throw new GraphQlInputException(__('Payflow Pro is not available.'));
+        }
+        // END PATCH
+
         $cart = $this->getCartForUser->execute($maskedCartId, $context->getUserId(), $storeId);
 
         $paypalPayload = $args['input']['paypal_payload'] ?? '';
